## Part 1 — How the data flows

```
  JotForm forms                Google Sheet (4 tabs)
        |                              |
        | JotForm API                  | gspread
        v                              v
  get_submissions()            Locations   <- the master site list
        |                      Aliases     <- submitted value -> master name
        v                      Overrides   <- per-site quota changes
   extract_row()               Operating Days <- which days a site is open
        |                              |
        |  normalize_location() <-------'  (uses Aliases)
        v
   one row per submission
        |
        +--> compute_period_targets()  -> Compliance Summary -> Leaderboard
        +--> build_detail_table()      -> the "who" tables (names)
        +--> build_location_health()   -> Location Health tab
        +--> Excel export
```

### The one thing that causes most problems

A submission is only counted if its location text **exactly matches** a name
on the master list. Not "close to". Exactly, after trimming spaces and
decoding HTML entities.

There are two kinds of location dropdown in JotForm:

- **Reusable dropdown** — fed by the master location table in JotForm. Values
  match the master list automatically. Six forms use this.
- **Static list** — a list typed into the form by hand years ago. It drifts
  the moment anyone adds or renames a site. Four forms still use this:
  **Lot Audit**, **Parking/Work Area Hazard**, **Valet Driver Assessment**,
  **Shuttle Driver Assessment**.

When a static form sends `FL - Embassy Downtown Tampa` and the master list
says `FL - Embassy Tampa Downtown`, the submission matches nothing and is
thrown away silently. Nobody gets an error. The site just reads 0%.

**Aliases are the fix.** An alias says "when a form sends *this*, count it as
*that*". They live in the `Aliases` tab of the Google Sheet and are added from
the Location Health tab in the app. No code change, no deploy.

### Why pulls are cached, and why aliases are applied separately

Pulling from JotForm is the slow part. Lot Audit alone is around 90,000
submissions. So:

- **Forms are fetched concurrently**, four at a time. First pull is roughly
  three to four times faster than it used to be.
- **The result is cached for 20 minutes**, keyed on the forms and date range.
  Re-running the same report, opening Location Health, or downloading the
  Excel costs nothing extra.
- **Aliases are applied *after* the cache, on every render.** This is the
  subtle part and it is deliberate. If aliasing happened during extraction it
  would be baked into the cached rows, so saving an alias would appear to do
  nothing for 20 minutes. Instead the cache stores only `location_raw`, and
  `apply_location_aliases()` resolves it fresh each time. Save an alias and
  the numbers change immediately, with no re-pull.
- **"Force fresh pull"** on the Report tab bypasses the cache when you need
  submissions from the last few minutes.

Errors are never cached. A failed pull does not wedge a bad result in place.

The permanent fix is moving those four forms onto the reusable dropdown in the
JotForm builder. That is a known future task. Until it happens, aliases are
not a workaround, they are how the system works.

