## Part 4 — Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Most likely cause | Fix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A site shows 0% | Its name is not in that form's dropdown, so nobody there can submit | Check the form's dropdown in the JotForm builder before treating it as a compliance failure |
| A site shows 0% and Location Health lists a similar-looking value | Static dropdown drift | Add an alias |
| Everything shows 0 and there is a red "No locations are loaded" banner | The Google Sheet is unreachable, or the `Locations` tab is empty | Check `overrides_sheet_url`, and that the sheet is shared with the service account's `client_email` |
| Name columns are blank on a detail form | The form was cloned and its fields renamed | Debug → Field names, then add the real name to that form's `fields` list |
| A change to the sheet has not shown up | The sheet loads once per session | Click **Reload from Google Sheet** in the sidebar |
| A submission made minutes ago is missing | The pull is cached for 20 minutes | Tick **Force fresh pull** and re-run |
| Red banner about the form registry | A typo in `FORMS` | The banner names the exact problem |
| Quota override seems ignored | The Quota cell is blank | Blank means "ignored". Enter `0` for "not required". |
| First report of the day is slow | Lot Audit alone is ~90,000 submissions, and the cache is cold | Narrow the date range, or deselect forms you do not need. Repeat runs within 20 minutes are instant. |
| `JotForm API error ... 401` | Bad or revoked API key | Rotate it in Secrets |

